<CasaPi title="Terms of use" description="Scope and limitations of the personal CasaPi Air Quality integration.">
<p>Effective October 7, 2026. CasaPi Air Quality is Andy Chiu’s experimental personal home automation integration. It is not offered as a public service and has no public registration or subscription fee.</p>
<h2>Authorized use</h2><p>Only connect devices you own or are authorized to manage. The account owner controls Google permissions and may revoke them at any time. Use of Google and other connected services remains subject to their applicable terms.</p>
<h2>Limitations</h2><p>Sensor reception, network access, Google authorization, and device behavior can fail or change. CasaPi is provided as available, without a promise of uninterrupted operation or a particular air-quality outcome. It is not a smoke alarm, carbon-monoxide detector, medical device, or substitute for suitable ventilation. Users remain responsible for household equipment settings and monitoring.</p>
<h2>Privacy and contact</h2><p>Data handling is described in the <a href="/casapi/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. Contact <a href="mailto:theandychiu+website@gmail.com">Andy Chiu</a> with questions or to request disconnection. These terms do not exclude rights that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>
